{"name":"Winter Solstice","hex":"#49545c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winter solstice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The point in Earth's orbital path at which either the Northern or Southern Hemisphere is maximally tilted away from the Sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winter_solstice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winter solstice","blocks":[{"text":"The winter solstice, or hibernal solstice, occurs when either of Earth's poles reaches its maximum tilt away from the Sun. This happens twice yearly, once in each hemisphere. For that hemisphere, the winter solstice is the day with the shortest period of daylight and longest night of the year, and when the Sun is at its lowest arc in the sky. In each polar region, there is continuous darkness or twilight around its winter solstice. The opposite event is the summer solstice, which happens at the same time in the opposite hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Stonehege_%282148722919%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Stonehege_%282148722919%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_solstice"},{"title":"Winter Solstice (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Winter Solstice is a 2004 American drama film written and directed by Josh Sternfeld and starring Anthony LaPaglia, Aaron Stanford, and Mark Webber. The story focuses on the efforts of a man to interact with and relate to his sons in the years following the accidental death of his wife."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/WinterSolsticePoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_Solstice_(film)"},{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt of Earth's axis. Different cultures define different dates as the start of winter, and some use a definition based on weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/330px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter"},{"title":"Solstice","blocks":[{"text":"A solstice is the time when the Sun reaches its most northerly or southerly sun path relative to the celestial equator on the celestial sphere. Two solstices occur annually, around 20–22 June and 20–22 December. In many countries, the seasons of the year are defined by reference to the solstices and the equinoxes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solstice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/1280px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view of Earth on the Northern hemisphere's winter solstice, with the North pole tilted furthest away from the Sun","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/2013_Solstice_Newgrange.jpg/500px-2013_Solstice_Newgrange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/2013_Solstice_Newgrange.jpg/500px-2013_